{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BringsSurface.lagrange_resolvent_transform","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.lagrange_resolvent_transform","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Complex.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.lagrange_resolvent_transform","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.lagrange_resolvent_transform","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/lagrange_resolvent_transform.lean#L79-L89","doc":"**Lagrange resolvent transform** ([`prop:lagrange-resolvent-transform`]).\n\nBundles the equivariance claim as the main statement; item (ii)\non `C_n`-invariant polynomials is recorded in the docstring. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:lagrange-resolvent-transform","label":"prop:lagrange-resolvent-transform","md":"quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/lagrange-resolvent-transform.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.lagrange_resolvent_transform_equivariance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.lagrange_resolvent_transform_equivariance","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/lagrange_resolvent_transform.lean#L63-L77","doc":"**(i) Diagonal action of the cyclic shift on Fourier modes**\n([`prop:lagrange-resolvent-transform`] item (i)).\n\nThe cyclic-shift action becomes a phase rotation on the `w_k`:\n`(L ∘ σ)(x) k = ζ^{-k} · (L x) k`,  i.e.\n`w_k(σ x) = ζ^{-k} · w_k(x)`.\n\nConditional on `[LagrangeResolventEquivarianceAxiom]` (§3b-cond). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.LagrangeResolventEquivarianceAxiom.claim_equivariance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.LagrangeResolventEquivarianceAxiom.claim_equivariance","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/lagrange_resolvent_transform.lean#L59-L59","doc":"Manuscript identity: `w_k(σ x) = ζ^{-k} · w_k(x)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.LagrangeResolventEquivarianceAxiom.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.LagrangeResolventEquivarianceAxiom.mk","kind":"ctor","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/lagrange_resolvent_transform.lean#L57-L57","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.LagrangeResolventEquivarianceAxiom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.LagrangeResolventEquivarianceAxiom","kind":"class","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/lagrange_resolvent_transform.lean#L54-L61","doc":"§3b-cond axiomatisation of the Lagrange-resolvent equivariance:\nthe cyclic-shift action becomes a phase rotation on the\nFourier modes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.cyclicShift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.cyclicShift","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/lagrange_resolvent_transform.lean#L49-L52","doc":"The cyclic-shift action `σ : (x_j) ↦ (x_{j+1})` on `Fin n → ℂ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.lagrangeResolventTransform","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.lagrangeResolventTransform","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/lagrange_resolvent_transform.lean#L43-L47","doc":"The Lagrange resolvent transform `(x_j) ↦ (w_k)` on `Fin n → ℂ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.rootOfUnity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.rootOfUnity","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/lagrange_resolvent_transform.lean#L39-L41","doc":"The primitive `n`-th root of unity `ζ_n = exp(2πi/n)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}